					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "MANUAL INSTANTIATION\n\nLet's start with a tiny recap of the fundamentals tutorial.\n\nMost nodes in Wire can be instantiated, either by connecting an instantiated signal to an inlet or by manually setting the instance count on the node or in the node panel.\n\nNodes will always update their instance count to the largest collection they receive, smaller collections will be repeated until they match the largest collection.\n\nAssignment: Create a color node, instantiate it two times and set it to two different colors. Then connect it to the color inlet on the Shape Render node. Remember: you can CMD\/CTRL + Click on an instantiated value box to open up the collection widget."
					}
				},
